# Calculus: area under a curve grows as the right edge moves.
title "An integral is accumulated area"
schema axes x=[0,4] y=[0,10]

mark f path fn={0.5*x^2 + 1} label="f(x)"
mark area region of=f from=0 to=0.2 label="area"
mark A label value={integral(f, 0, area.to)} label="area so far"

Say: "Here is a curve. Shade the area under it, starting at zero."
focus area
Say: "Push the right edge |sweep| out to three, and the area accumulates."
@sweep morph area.to 0.2 -> 3 4s ease=linear
focus A
Say: "From zero to three the area is seven and a half."
focus none
